items.description:
mapping between SDF filter from PCC rules and NAS QoS rules. 
Especially interesting how you define the filter for the UE

@phine_stefan is already working on a SDF filter parsing, but the second part is still missing

For example with below UDR information I am not able to create two PDU session

INSERT INTO `SessionManagementSubscriptionData` (`ueid`, `servingPlmnid`, `singleNssai`, `dnnConfigurations`) VALUES
('505010000000032', '5051', '{\"sst\": 1, \"sd\": \"16777215\"}','{\"internet\":{\"pduSessionTypes\":{ \"defaultSessionType\": \"IPV4\"},\"sscModes\": {\"defaultSscMode\": \"SSC_MODE_1\"},\"5gQosProfile\": {\"5qi\": 1,\"arp\":{\"priorityLevel\": 15,\"preemptCap\": \"NOT_PREEMPT\",\"preemptVuln\":\"PREEMPTABLE\"},\"priorityLevel\":1},\"sessionAmbr\":{\"uplink\":\"1000Mbps\", \"downlink\":\"1000Mbps\"},\"staticIpAddress\":[{\"ipv4Addr\": \"12.1.1.13\"}]},\"ims\":{\"pduSessionTypes\":{ \"defaultSessionType\": \"IPV4V6\"},\"sscModes\": {\"defaultSscMode\": \"SSC_MODE_1\"},\"5gQosProfile\": {\"5qi\": 2,\"arp\":{\"priorityLevel\": 15,\"preemptCap\": \"NOT_PREEMPT\",\"preemptVuln\":\"PREEMPTABLE\"},\"priorityLevel\":1},\"sessionAmbr\":{\"uplink\":\"1000Mbps\", \"downlink\":\"1000Mbps\"}}}');

The 5qi should be taken from UDR directly or from the SMF conf file if we configure local information. Right now it is hard-coded 

